Upstream @refinedev/hasura 7.0.1 merges a read's sorters into one order_by object:
generateSorting spreads each sorter's object into the one before it. A GraphQL server
coerces an input object in its input type's own field order, not in the order its keys
were written, so an order_by object carries no priority: a list read sorted by two keys
or more is ordered by whichever key its order_by type declares first, and two sorters
under one relation overwrite each other. Hasura's own multi-column sort is a list.

This patch makes generateSorting return a list, one object per sorter in the order
given, a dotted field nested as before; no sorters still give undefined. getList's
non-default naming path converts each entry of that list. The ESM and CommonJS builds,
the declarations of generateSorting and the shipped sources change the same lines in
place, so the source maps keep their positions; the source text they embed still shows
the stock functions. Remove the patch and its install-policy entry when the first
@refinedev/hasura release that sends sorters as a list is adopted.

